.TH PKRAM 1 "2026-09-01" "pkram 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pkram \- track Papierkram work time from the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pkram
.I subcommand
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pkram
lists projects and tasks, creates and deletes time entries, and runs a local
timer against the Papierkram API, without opening the web interface.
.PP
It is an unofficial third-party tool and is not affiliated with, endorsed by,
or supported by the makers of Papierkram.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B auth set-token [\-\-stdin]
Store the API token in the macOS Keychain. Prompts with terminal echo disabled,
or reads from standard input with \fB\-\-stdin\fR.
.TP
.B auth status
Report whether a token is stored, and for which subdomain. Never prints the token.
.TP
.B auth check
Verify that the stored token authenticates against the API.
.TP
.B auth delete [\-\-force]
Remove the stored token from the Keychain.
.TP
.B projects list [\-\-all] [\-\-company \fIid\fR]
List projects.
.TP
.B tasks list [\-\-project \fIid\fR]
List tasks, optionally limited to one project.
.TP
.B entries list [\-\-from \fIdate\fR] [\-\-to \fIdate\fR] [\-\-project \fIid\fR] [\-\-task \fIname\fR|\fIid\fR]
List time entries. Dates accept \fBYYYY-MM-DD\fR, \fBtoday\fR, \fByesterday\fR or
\fBtomorrow\fR. Unlike the writing subcommands, this does \fInot\fR inherit
\fBtask_id\fR from \fB.pkram\fR: a listing narrowed to a single task cannot be
told apart from a day with nothing booked.
.TP
.B entries add \-\-start \fIHH:MM\fR \-\-end \fIHH:MM\fR [\-\-date \fIdate\fR] [\-\-task \fIname\fR|\fIid\fR] [\-\-comment \fItext\fR] [\-\-unbillable] [\-\-force]
Create a time entry. Without \fB\-\-force\fR it resolves customer, project and
task and asks for confirmation first.
.TP
.B entries delete \fIid\fR [\-\-force]
Delete a time entry.
.TP
.B timer start [\-\-task \fIname\fR|\fIid\fR] [\-\-comment \fItext\fR]
Start a local timer. The timer lives on this machine until it is stopped.
.TP
.B timer status
Show the running timer.
.TP
.B timer stop [\-\-dry\-run] [\-\-force]
Stop the timer and submit it as a time entry.
.TP
.B timer cancel [\-\-force]
Discard the running timer without writing anything.
.TP
.B config show
Print the effective configuration and where it came from.
.TP
.B config set \fIkey\fR \fIvalue\fR
Set \fBsubdomain\fR or \fBdefault-user-id\fR in the user configuration.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.B pkram
reads an optional
.B .pkram
file from the current directory, and from parent directories up to the
enclosing git root. Example:
.PP
.RS
.nf
{
  "subdomain": "your-subdomain",
  "company_id": 1,
  "project_id": 2,
  "task_id": 3,
  "tasks": { "tickets": 4, "maintenance": 3 },
  "user_id": 1
}
.fi
.RE
.PP
.B task_id
is the default for
.B entries add
and
.BR "timer start" .
Tasks listed under
.B tasks
can be addressed by name wherever a task is expected, so
.B \-\-task tickets
is equivalent to
.BR "\-\-task 4" .
.PP
Precedence, highest first:
.PP
.RS
command-line flag, \fBPAPIERKRAM_*\fR environment, \fB.pkram\fR, user config
.RE
.PP
There is no built-in default subdomain. Without one,
.B pkram
refuses to run rather than address somebody else's tenant.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.config/pkram/config.json
User configuration. Honours \fBXDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR.
.TP
.B ~/.local/state/pkram/timer.json
The running local timer. Honours \fBXDG_STATE_HOME\fR.
.TP
.B ./.pkram
Per-project configuration.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PAPIERKRAM_SUBDOMAIN, PAPIERKRAM_USER_ID, PAPIERKRAM_COMPANY_ID, PAPIERKRAM_PROJECT_ID, PAPIERKRAM_TASK_ID
Override the corresponding configuration values.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable ANSI colours.
.SH SECURITY
The API token is kept in the macOS Keychain under service
.BR papierkram-api-key ,
with the subdomain as the account. It is never written to disk by
.BR pkram .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B pkram
exits 0 on success and non-zero on error.
.SH AUTHOR
Written by Vanille Media.
